\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces The QFVM pipeline for the one-dimensional compressible Euler equations. Flow fields are served coherently from a QRAM; Roe flux formulas written as pure Python are compiled to reversible arithmetic; the implicit-step operator is exposed as a sparse-access oracle pair; and the linear solve is an \emph  {injected} QLSS kernel operating under an explicit spectral promise. Its fixed-point physics is certified against an independent fixed-point semantics in the verification matrix of Section~\ref {sec:implementation}.}}{32}{figure.caption.51}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:qfvm}{{9}{32}{The QFVM pipeline for the one-dimensional compressible Euler equations. Flow fields are served coherently from a QRAM; Roe flux formulas written as pure Python are compiled to reversible arithmetic; the implicit-step operator is exposed as a sparse-access oracle pair; and the linear solve is an \emph {injected} QLSS kernel operating under an explicit spectral promise. Its fixed-point physics is certified against an independent fixed-point semantics in the verification matrix of \secref {sec:implementation}}{figure.caption.51}{}}
